# Security headers, shared by every static host that reads a `_headers` file
# from the publish directory: Netlify (dailymilk.netlify.app) and Cloudflare
# Pages (dailymilk.pages.dev).
#
# GitHub Pages (dailymilk.rajatmalik.dev, the primary site) ignores this file -
# it does not support custom response headers at all - so its headers have to be
# added at the DNS/CDN layer. See "Security headers" in README.md.
#
# `preload` is inert on *.netlify.app and *.pages.dev: the preload list operates
# at the registrable-domain level and neither domain is ours to submit. It only
# becomes meaningful on a custom domain, where it also commits every subdomain
# to HTTPS - do not submit until that is true everywhere.
#
# Content-Security-Policy mirrors the <meta http-equiv> policy in src/index.html,
# which is not negotiable: `ng build` adds a second, hash-based policy and the
# browser enforces the intersection of all of them. The only extra directive is
# frame-ancestors, which <meta> cannot express - it is the header-only half of
# the clickjacking protection that X-Frame-Options also provides.
# src/security-headers.spec.ts fails if this drifts from src/index.html.
#
# X-XSS-Protection is ignored by every current browser; it is kept because
# security scanners still look for it.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=()
